{
  "board": { "name": "Cold Email Engine", "color": "#34D399" },
  "columns": [
    {
      "name": "Research",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "CAN-SPAM (US) legal requirements",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "**No B2B exemption.** Required: accurate From/To/Reply-To/routing headers, non-deceptive subject lines, **valid physical postal address in every message**, functional opt-out honored within **10 business days**, monitor third parties. Opt-out model (no prior consent needed). Penalty up to **$53,088 per email** (2025); FTC Verkada $2.95M (Aug 2024). Source: FTC compliance guide, adaptivesecurity.com."
        },
        {
          "title": "GDPR + ePrivacy (EU) legal requirements",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Lawful basis for B2B cold email is usually **legitimate interest Art. 6(1)(f)** with a documented **LIA (Purpose/Necessity/Balancing)**. Must be relevant to recipient's professional role, identify sender, working opt-out. **Country variance:** Germany (UWG) often needs prior consent even B2B; France (CNIL) allows LI but strict opt-out; UK/many allow corporate-address exemption. Rights: access/erasure, retention limits, processor DPAs. Fines €500–€900k+ (SOLOCAL, CNIL 2025)."
        },
        {
          "title": "CASL (Canada) legal requirements",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Strictest — consent-based. **Express or implied consent** (EBR: purchase/contract 24mo, inquiry 6mo; OR conspicuously published business email with no anti-CEM statement + relevant). If profile says 'no cold email' → excluded. Every msg: consent + sender ID + working unsubscribe (10 business days). **Keep consent records 3 years.** Penalties up to **$1M individual / $10M org**; CRTC 2025 settlements $15k–$75k, auditing B2B tools."
        },
        {
          "title": "Scraping vs licensed data — legal assessment",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Collection vs use are distinct legal events. US: scraping public data not generally illegal (hiQ v LinkedIn) unless site ToS forbids it (ToS/CFAA-adjacent risk). **Use-side liability remains** (CAN-SPAM/GDPR/CASL). **Google Maps/Places forbids scraping + >30-day caching.** Recommendation: default to licensed providers (DPAs, refreshable, vendor shares compliance); treat scraping as opt-in, per-source ToS-reviewed, gated through suppression+verification."
        },
        {
          "title": "Data provider APIs — capabilities & pricing",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "**Apollo.io** 275M+ contacts, from ~$49/mo, internal-use-only ToS (no resale/share), GDPR DPA. **Hunter.io** email find/verify from ~$34/mo. **People Data Labs** 1.5B+ profiles, ~$98/mo, ~$0.01/record, pure API. **Clearbit** (HubSpot Breeze) firmographic. **RocketReach/Lusha/Snov** fallbacks. **Google Places (New)** local firmographics — per-SKU free caps + $100/$275/$1,200 tiers; rarely returns email."
        },
        {
          "title": "Sending infra & ESP policy comparison",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "**Amazon SES** ~$0.10/1k, dedicated IP ~$24.95/mo, permissive incl. cold — primary at scale. **Postmark** rejects cold email (opt-in only) — system/transactional only. **SendGrid** flexible, shared-pool variable, free tier gone 2025. **Nxeon Mail (Mailcow)** self-hosted, brand-owned domains, **DKIM via Mailcow API** (not local resolver). Abstract a MailTransport interface."
        },
        {
          "title": "Deliverability: SPF/DKIM/DMARC, warmup, caps",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Gmail/Yahoo (2024) require SPF+DKIM+DMARC for bulk (>5k/day). Warmup 5–15/day ramp over 3–6 wks to **safe ceiling 30–50/inbox/day** (cap includes warmup). Keep bounce <2%, Gmail spam complaint <**0.3%**. Verify every address before first send. Separate warmup vs live traffic in scheduling."
        },
        {
          "title": "RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe requirement",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Gmail/Yahoo require **List-Unsubscribe + List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click** for bulk senders since Feb–Jun 2024. HTTPS endpoint, POST unsubscribes with no confirmation, honored within **48h**. We honor immediately + write suppression. Sources: Valimail, Mailgun, Postmark, EmailLabs."
        },
        {
          "title": "Competitor teardown (Instantly/Smartlead/Lemlist/Apollo)",
          "label": "research",
          "body": "Instantly ~$97/mo, ~78% placement, volume+simplicity. Smartlead ~$94/seat, ~85% (best), SmartDelivery. Lemlist ~$69/seat, ~62%, personalization. Apollo all-in-one data+sending ~$49–$395. Our edge: own data+engine across 3 brands, compliance as differentiator, Nxeon Mail integration."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ideas",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Cross-brand frequency cap",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Prevent the same person receiving near-simultaneous cold emails from Nxeon + Agency + Ads Autopilot. Enforce one brand per contact per N days. Protects reputation + recipient trust."
        },
        {
          "title": "Complaint-rate circuit breaker",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Auto-pause a domain/campaign when spam-complaint rate approaches Gmail's 0.3% threshold or bounce >2%. Alert admin. Prevents cascade blacklisting across shared brands."
        },
        {
          "title": "AI personalization tokens (opt-in)",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Dynamic first-line/merge tokens per business vertical (Lemlist-style) — but never at the expense of deliverability. Gate behind template lint."
        },
        {
          "title": "Deliverability/warmup dashboard",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Per-domain reputation, warmup state, daily cap usage, bounce/complaint trend, Postmaster signals. Surface in both standalone app and Nxeon admin add-on."
        },
        {
          "title": "Places local-vertical discovery module",
          "label": "idea",
          "body": "Use Google Places (New) to discover local businesses by vertical/geo for list-building. Must refresh/purge content within 30 days (ToS), store only place_id long-term, source email elsewhere."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Backlog",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Enrichment pipeline (Hunter verify + Apollo/PDL pull)",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "EnrichmentJob abstraction: pull firmographics/contacts from Apollo/PDL, verify emails via Hunter, track cost + records in/out. Internal-use-only per provider ToS. Feed enrichmentStatus + emailVerifiedStatus on Contact."
        },
        {
          "title": "Dynamic list / segment builder",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Save filters over Business+Contact store (category, type, size, vertical, geo, legalBasis, verification). Dynamic vs static lists. Powers list-building across many verticals."
        },
        {
          "title": "Mailbox rotation pools",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Rotate across multiple SendingIdentities/mailboxes per brand to spread volume under per-inbox caps. Jittered, throttled scheduling."
        },
        {
          "title": "Bounce & complaint ingestion (SES/Mailcow FBL)",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Consume SES notifications + Mailcow feedback/FBL. Hard bounce/complaint → auto-suppress. Wire into circuit breaker."
        },
        {
          "title": "DSAR / GDPR erasure workflow",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Data-subject access + erasure: tombstone the contact while preserving a hashed suppression entry so they're never re-contacted. Audit-logged."
        },
        {
          "title": "Provider cost tracking + Places 30-day refresh",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "ProviderPull records with cost + expiry. Enforce Google Places 30-day cache purge/refresh; only place_id persists. Dashboard of monthly data spend."
        },
        {
          "title": "Analytics: open/click/reply funnel per brand+campaign",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Aggregate immutable Events into per-brand, per-campaign, per-sequence-step funnels. Reply detection + positive-reply flagging."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Phase 1",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Prisma schema — full data model",
          "label": "foundation",
          "body": "Model Brand, SendingIdentity, SendingDomain, Business, Contact, List/ListMember, Campaign, Sequence/Step, Template, Send, Event, Suppression, ConsentRecord, AuditLog, EnrichmentJob. Separate DB from /opt/nxeon; integrate via API only."
        },
        {
          "title": "Compliance primitives FIRST (suppression + consent + unsub)",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Build Suppression (unique on brandScope+emailHash, checked at queue AND send time), ConsentRecord (retained 3yr), and RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe endpoint + hosted preference page before any sending path exists."
        },
        {
          "title": "Brand + SendingIdentity + verified domain setup",
          "label": "foundation",
          "body": "Per-brand physical postal address, From identity, domains with SPF/DKIM/DMARC verification gate (DKIM via Mailcow API for Nxeon Mail). A domain cannot send until verified."
        },
        {
          "title": "MVP outreach loop (single brand: Nxeon)",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Manual Business+Contact import, static list, Campaign→Sequence→Template, SES/Mailcow transport, per-domain caps + warmup, open/click/reply/bounce/complaint tracking."
        },
        {
          "title": "Template lint (CAN-SPAM enforcement)",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Block send unless template contains injected physical postal address + working unsubscribe block, honest From, non-deceptive subject. Hard gate at campaign activation."
        },
        {
          "title": "Sending scheduler with per-domain/day caps + warmup ramp",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Throttled, jittered queue. Enforce 30–50/inbox/day ceiling incl. warmup traffic. Ramp new domains 5–15/day over 3–6 weeks. Separate warmup vs live counters."
        },
        {
          "title": "Tracking pipeline (open/click/reply/bounce/complaint)",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Pixel + wrapped links + reply/bounce/complaint ingestion → immutable Event log. Auto-suppress on hard bounce/complaint/unsubscribe."
        },
        {
          "title": "Standalone Next.js app scaffold on 51.79.226.215",
          "label": "foundation",
          "body": "App Router + TS + Prisma + Postgres, own auth, deploy on dev box. Core screens: Businesses, Contacts, Lists, Campaigns, Templates, Domains, Suppression, Compliance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Later",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Multi-brand: all three sending identities",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Nxeon + Marketing Agency + Ads Autopilot each with own domains/identities/templates/address, sharing the engine + global suppression. Optional brand-scoped suppression tier under global."
        },
        {
          "title": "Jurisdiction-aware consent gate",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Country-aware send gate: GDPR LIA workflow, CASL 24mo/6mo windows + anti-CEM statement checks, Germany express-consent block. Store legalBasis/jurisdiction/consentSource/expiry per contact."
        },
        {
          "title": "Nxeon admin add-on module (/admin/coldemail)",
          "label": "integration",
          "body": "Mount module in Nxeon portal matching brand theme (navy/violet/cyan). Server-to-server signed token; heavy ops proxy to standalone service; embed dashboards + campaign controls. Publish compliance/suppression state back to hub."
        },
        {
          "title": "Warmup automation + reputation scoring",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Automated warmup pool, per-domain reputationScore, Postmaster Tools integration, auto-throttle on degraded reputation."
        },
        {
          "title": "Deliverability analytics + Postmaster integration",
          "label": "feature",
          "body": "Track inbox placement, spam-complaint rate (<0.3%), authentication pass rates per domain. Feed circuit breaker."
        },
        {
          "title": "Audit export + retention policy engine",
          "label": "compliance",
          "body": "Exportable AuditLog + ConsentRecord retention (≥3yr CASL), automated retention/erasure schedules per jurisdiction."
        },
        {
          "title": "Docs: DOCUMENTATION.md + /admin/docs mirror",
          "label": "integration",
          "body": "Per Nxeon workflow, keep DOCUMENTATION.md current with every change and mirror into admin /admin/docs (public /docs retired)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Done",
      "cards": [
        {
          "title": "Research round complete — architecture.md written",
          "label": "milestone",
          "body": "Compliance (CAN-SPAM/GDPR+ePrivacy/CASL), data sourcing (providers + pricing + ToS), sending infra + deliverability, competitors, full data model, multi-brand + Nxeon add-on wiring, phased plan, risks. Sources cited. No code/DB/sends per guardrails."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
